#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:19
#, no-c-format
msgid "&ktimemon; is a system monitor for the K Desktop Environment"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: keyword
#: ktimemon.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid "<keyword>KDE</keyword>"
msgstr "<keyword>KDE</keyword>"

#. Tag: keyword
#: ktimemon.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid "ktimemon"
msgstr "Ktimemon"

#. Tag: keyword
#: ktimemon.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid "system monitor"
msgstr "ការ​គ្រប់គ្រង​ប្រព័ន្ធ"

#. Tag: keyword
#: ktimemon.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid "timemon"
msgstr "timemon"

#. Tag: title
#: ktimemon.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "សេចក្ដី​ណែនាំ"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ktimemon; is a small program to keep track of your computer's system usage. It "
"can display bar graphs containing information about <acronym>CPU</acronym>"
", memory, and swap usage as well as disk usage and context switch activity. In "
"keeping with the spirit of <ulink url=\"http://www.kde.org/\">KDE</ulink>"
", it supports configuration via a graphical user interface. It also supports "
"<emphasis>docking</emphasis>, &ie; it can display information in the system "
"panel tray."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:40
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Currently, &ktimemon; only supports a limited number of systems: &Linux; based "
"installations with the <filename>/proc</filename> file system, &Solaris; based "
"installations with the <filename>kstat</filename> library, and Digital &UNIX; "
"(formerly DEC/OSF1) based installations with the <command>table</command>"
"(2) system call. Help with porting it to other platforms is most welcome."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:50
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ktimemon; can be started from the command line or from the &kde; <guimenu>"
"start</guimenu> menu (in the <guisubmenu>Utilities</guisubmenu> "
"submenu). If you choose to start from the command line, &ktimemon; honors the "
"usual &X-Window; program flags such as <option>-geometry</option>"
". &ktimemon; is <emphasis>session-aware</emphasis>, &ie; it keeps track of the "
"current state (colors, &etc;) and restores it in the user's next session."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: ktimemon.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid "Onscreen Fundamentals"
msgstr "មូលដ្ឋាន​គ្រឹះ​លើ​អេក្រង់"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:63
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After starting &ktimemon; a small window will appear displaying information "
"gathered from the operating system. If you move the mouse pointer over the "
"&ktimemon; window and let it rest for a small amount of time, a <emphasis>"
"tool-tip</emphasis> (&ie; a small transient window) will appear. The tool-tip "
"contains numeric information about the system parameters displayed by the bar "
"graphs. Tool-tips can be disabled (refer to <link linkend=\"config\">"
"Configuration</link>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: ktimemon.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Display Modes"
msgstr "របៀប​បង្ហាញ"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ktimemon; can display two different sets of system information. As explained "
"in the <link linkend=\"config\">Configuration</link> "
"chapter, mouse buttons can be bound to various actions. Per default, the left "
"mouse button is bound to the mode switch action, &ie; by clicking the &LMB; "
"mouse button anywhere in the &ktimemon; window, the displayed information "
"switches from <guilabel>Normal Mode</guilabel> (the default) to <guilabel>"
"Extended Mode</guilabel>, and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: ktimemon.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "Normal Mode"
msgstr "របៀប​ធម្មតា"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After starting &ktimemon; for the first time, it will show information about "
"the current CPU activity, as well as memory and swap usage. Three bar graphs "
"are used to show this information; they are updated regularly (the default "
"sample interval is 0.5s, but it can be changed, see <link linkend=\"config\">"
"Configuration</link>). The three bar graphs represent (from left to right):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: ktimemon.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "<acronym>CPU</acronym> usage."
msgstr "ការ​ប្រើប្រាស់ <acronym>CPU</acronym> ។"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ktimemon; shows the bar in three different colors, representing <acronym>"
"CPU</acronym> time spent in various modes. From bottom to top they are: kernel "
"mode, user mode, and user mode with lowered priority (<emphasis>nice</emphasis>"
") - since &Solaris; does not seem to support statistics for nice mode, the "
"topmost part of the bar represents time spent in the <emphasis>wait</emphasis> "
"state on such systems. The gap from the top of the bar to the top of the window "
"represents the percentage the <acronym>CPU</acronym> idle time."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: ktimemon.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "Memory usage."
msgstr "ការ​ប្រើប្រាស់​សតិ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Similar to the <acronym>CPU</acronym> usage bar, this bar is composed of three "
"sub fields, representing (from bottom to top): memory allocated by processes, "
"memory used for I/O buffering, and memory used for file caching. For Digital "
"&UNIX; based systems, the middle section represents <quote>inactive</quote> "
"memory (&ie; memory allocated and not used for a certain amount of time), and "
"for &Solaris; based systems, the middle section of the bar is not used, and the "
"topmost section represents the amount of memory used by the kernel. Again, the "
"gap from the top of the bar to the top of the window represents free memory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: ktimemon.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "Swap usage."
msgstr "ការ​ប្រើប្រាស់​ស្វប ។"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This bar consists of a single field representing the current swap usage "
"relative to the system's total amount of swap space."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking the mouse button bound to <quote>mode switch</quote> "
"in the &ktimemon; window switches to <quote>Extended Mode</quote>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: ktimemon.docbook:141
#, no-c-format
msgid "Extended Mode"
msgstr "របៀប​ដែល​បាន​បន្ថែម"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this mode, the three bar graphs are used to display a different set of "
"system information. Again from left to right, they show:"
msgstr ""
"ក្នុង​របៀប​នេះ "
"ក្រាប​របារ​បី​ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើ​ដើម្បី​បង្ហាញ​សំណុំ​ព័ត៌មាន​ប្រព័ន្ធ​ខុស​គ្នា ។ "
"ម្ដង​ទៀត​ពី​ឆ្វេង​ទៅ​ស្ដាំ ពួក​វា​បង្ហាញ ៖"

#. Tag: term
#: ktimemon.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "Paging activity."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This bar consists of two parts, the lower half of which shows the number of "
"memory pages written to secondary storage in the last sample interval. "
"Similarly, the upper half indicates the number of pages read from secondary "
"storage."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: ktimemon.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid "Swapping activity."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid "The second bar displays the analog information for swap activity."
msgstr "របារ​ទីពីរ​បង្ហាញ​ព័ត៌មាន​អាណាឡូក​សម្រាប់​សកម្មភាព​ស្វប ។"

#. Tag: term
#: ktimemon.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid "Context switches."
msgstr "បរិបទ​ផ្លាស់ប្ដូរ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:166
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Again, this bar graph consists of a single field which indicates the number of "
"context switches in the last sample interval."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Since there is no <quote>natural</quote> way of scaling the information shown "
"in <quote>Extended Mode</quote>, by default &ktimemon; uses <emphasis>"
"autoscaling</emphasis> (explained in the <link linkend=\"autoscaling\">"
"Common Questions Section</link>). There is, however, the possibility of "
"specifying the scaling information, see the <link linkend=\"config\">"
"Configuration</link> section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Note that the two sets of bar graphs share the same colors, &ie; the colors "
"setup for <quote>Normal Mode</quote> is also used for displaying information in "
"<quote>Extended Mode</quote> (see also <link linkend=\"config\">"
"Configuration</link> on how to change the color scheme)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: ktimemon.docbook:190
#, no-c-format
msgid "Menu Structure"
msgstr "រចនា​សម្ព័ន្ធ​ម៉ឺនុយ"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By default, the &RMB; mouse button is bound to the <quote>menu pop-up</quote> "
"action, &ie; clicking the right mouse button anywhere in the &ktimemon; window "
"brings up a menu, which is discussed in the following sections."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: ktimemon.docbook:200
#, no-c-format
msgid "Settings..."
msgstr "ការ​កំណត់..."

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenuitem>Settings...</guimenuitem> menu item is used to pop up the "
"configuration dialog. Configuration options are discussed in section <link "
"linkend=\"config\">Configuration</link>."
msgstr ""
"ធាតុ​ម៉ឺនុយ <guimenuitem>ការ​កំណត់...</guimenuitem> "
"ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើ​ដើម្បី​ធ្វើ​ឲ្យ​លេចឡើង​ប្រអប់​ការ​កំណត់​រចនា​សម្ព័ន្ធ ។ "
"ជម្រើស​ការ​កំណត់​រចនា​សម្ព័ន្ធ​ត្រូវ​បាន​ពិភាក្សា​ក្នុង​ផ្នែក <link "
"linkend=\"config\">ការ​កំណត់​រចនា​សម្ព័ន្ធ</link> ។"

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: ktimemon.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "Docked In Panel"
msgstr "ដែល​ចូលចត​ក្នុង​បន្ទះ"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:211
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting the <guimenuitem>Docked In Panel</guimenuitem> "
"menu item, &ktimemon; switches between its standard display (&ie; a normal "
"window) and the panelized state, where the &ktimemon; window disappears and a "
"smaller version is displayed in the system panel. Apart from the reduction in "
"size, the <quote>panelized</quote> &ktimemon; behaves exactly like its big "
"brother."
msgstr ""
"ដោយ​ជ្រើស​ធាតុ​ម៉ឺនុយ <guimenuitem>ដែល​ចូលចត​ក្នុង​បន្ទះ</guimenuitem> "
"Ktimemon ប្ដូរ​រវាង​ការ​បង្ហាញ​ស្តង់ដារ​របស់​វា (ឧ. បង្អួច​ធម្មតា) "
"និង​ស្ថានភាព​ដែល​បាន​ពិន័យ ដែល​បង្អួច Ktimemon រលាយ​បាត់ "
"និង​កំណែ​តូច​ជាង​ត្រូវ​បាន​បង្ហាញ​ក្នុង​បន្ទះ​ប្រព័ន្ធ ។ "
"មួយ​ផ្នែក​ពី​ការ​កាត់​បន្ថយ​ក្នុង​ទំហំ Ktimemon <quote>ដែល​ពិន័យ</quote> "
"ធ្វើ​ឥរិយាបថ​ដូច​បង​ធំ​របស់​វា ។"

#. Tag: guimenu
#: ktimemon.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid "Help"
msgstr "ជំនួយ"

#. Tag: sect2
#: ktimemon.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid "&help.menu.documentation;"
msgstr "&help.menu.documentation;"

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: ktimemon.docbook:229
#, no-c-format
msgid "Horizontal Bars"
msgstr "របារ​ផ្ដេក"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:231
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By selecting the <guimenuitem>Horizontal Bars</guimenuitem> "
"menu entry, &ktimemon; switches from vertical bars to horizontal bars and vice "
"versa. Not very useful, but it was easy to implement ;-)"
msgstr ""
"ដោយ​ជ្រើស​ធាតុ​ម៉ឺនុយ <guimenuitem>របារ​ផ្ដេក</guimenuitem> "
"Ktimemon ប្ដូរ​ពី​របារ​បញ្ឈរ​ទៅ​របារ​ផ្ដេក និង​ត្រឡប់​មក​វិញ ។ "
"មិន​មែន​មាន​ប្រយោជន៍​ណាស់ ប៉ុន្តែ​វា​ងាយ​ស្រួល​សម្រាប់​ប្រតិបត្តិ ;-)"

#. Tag: guimenuitem
#: ktimemon.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quit"
msgstr "ចេញ"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem> menu item - surprise, surprise -- is used "
"to terminate &ktimemon;. It will save the current state (&eg; the color scheme, "
"window size, whether it is displayed in the panel) and restore the state in the "
"next invocation."
msgstr ""
"ធាតុ​ម៉ឺនុយ <guimenuitem>ចេញ</guimenuitem> - surprise, surprise -- "
"ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើ​ដើម្បី​បញ្ចប់ Ktimemon ។ វា​នឹង​រក្សា​ទុក​សភាព​បច្ចុប្បន្ន (ឧ. "
"ពណ៌​ចម្រុះ ទំហំ​បង្អួច ថា​តើ​វា​ត្រូវ​បានបង្ហាញ​ក្នុង​បន្ទះ) "
"និង​ស្ដារ​សភាព​ក្នុង next invocation."

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The configuration information is saved in the file <filename>$<envar>"
"HOME</envar>/.kde/share/config/ktimemonrc</filename>"
", where <filename class=\"directory\">$<envar>HOME</envar></filename> "
"refers to the user's home folder. If this file is deleted, &ktimemon; will "
"start in its default state in the next invocation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: ktimemon.docbook:258
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configuration"
msgstr "ការ​កំណត់​រចនា​សម្ព័ន្ធ"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:260
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ktimemon; can be configured via a straight-forward dialog (see also the "
"discussion of the <link linkend=\"config-menu\">Configuration Menu</link>"
"). On the <guilabel>General</guilabel> page, the sample interval can be "
"specified as well as scaling information (see also the discussion of the <link "
"linkend=\"xtndmode\">extended mode</link>). If the <guilabel>"
"Autoscaling</guilabel> check box is ticked (autoscaling is explained in the "
"<link linkend=\"autoscaling\">FAQ</link> section), the scaling factors cannot "
"be edited, since &ktimemon; determines them automatically."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:272
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Colors</guilabel> page can be used to tailor the colors of the "
"bar graph to individual preferences. A small sample bar graph gives immediate "
"feedback."
msgstr ""
"ទំព័រ <guilabel>ពណ៌</guilabel> "
"អាច​ត្រូវ​បាន​ប្រើ​ដើម្បី​បន្ថែម​បន្ថយ​ពណ៌​នៃ​ក្រាប​របារ​ចំពោះ​ចំណូល​ចិត្ត​នីមួយ"
"ៗ ។ ក្រាប​របារ​គំរូ​តូច​ផ្ដល់​មតិ​ព័ត៌មាន​ភ្លាមៗ ។"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Interaction</guilabel> page, mouse bindings can be adapted. "
"Clicking a mouse button on the &ktimemon; window can be ignored, trigger a mode "
"switch (see also <link linkend=\"modes\">Modes</link>"
"), invoke the context menu (see also <link linkend=\"menu\">Menu</link>"
"), or invoke an external process. The command line specified for external "
"processes is interpreted by the standard shell, &ie; shell commands, "
"environment variables, redirection &etc; can be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:288
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Interaction</guilabel> page also contains a check box which can "
"be used to disable to automatic appearance of tool-tips with numeric "
"information about the bar graphs (compare <link linkend=\"fund\">"
"Onscreen Fundamentals</link>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: ktimemon.docbook:295
#, no-c-format
msgid "Common Questions and Answers"
msgstr "សំណួរ និង​ចម្លើយ​ទូទៅ"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:300
#, no-c-format
msgid "Which operating systems does &ktimemon; support?"
msgstr "តើ​ប្រព័ន្ធ​ប្រតិបត្តិការ​មួយ​ណា​ដែល Ktimemon គាំទ្រ?"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:303
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&ktimemon; supports &Linux; based systems with the <filename "
"class=\"devicefile\">/proc</filename> file system, &Solaris; based systems with "
"the <filename>kstat</filename> library, and Digital &UNIX; (formerly DEC/OSF1) "
"systems with the <command>table</command>(2) system call interface. Only the "
"&Linux; version has been thoroughly tested, if you experience any problems with "
"the &Solaris;/Digital &UNIX; port, please do not hesitate to contact me."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Also, contributions to &ktimemon; to adapt it to other platforms are most "
"welcome. Please contact me at <email>m.maierhofer@tees.ac.uk</email> "
"if you intend to port &ktimemon; to other flavors of &UNIX;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:326
#, no-c-format
msgid "How does autoscaling work?"
msgstr "តើ​ការ​ធ្វើ​មាត្រដ្ឋាន​ស្វ័យ​ប្រវត្តិ​ធ្វើ​ការ​របៀប​ណា?"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Glad you asked. Since there is no sensible predetermined scaling factor for "
"paging/swapping operations and context switches (unlike &eg; memory "
"utilization, where you can take the total memory size as baseline), &ktimemon; "
"uses a semi-intelligent (well, ...) autoscaling mechanism. Autoscaling works as "
"follows:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each of the three bar graphs as described in the <link linkend=\"xtndmode\">"
"extended mode section</link> has an associated scaling factor. The initial "
"values of these factors are set to some predetermined value."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each time a new sample is displayed, the respective value is tentatively scaled "
"with the corresponding factor. If the value can be displayed in the scale "
"chosen by the factor, no change occurs (&ie; small changes in the activity are "
"reflected by a changing height of the bar)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the scaled value would be either too large or too small to be displayed with "
"the current scaling factor, the scaling is adjusted so that the new value "
"displayed is roughly halfway up the bar graph. Thus, subsequent changes should "
"have a good chance of getting displayed relative to the current value, without "
"having to change the scale again."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:371
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Why does a message box with <errorname>diagnostic output from child "
"command</errorname> pop up?"
msgstr ""
"ហេតុ​អ្វី​ប្រអប់​សារ​ដែល​មាន "
"<errorname>ទិន្នផល​វិនិច្ឆ័យ​ពី​ពាក្យ​បញ្ជា​កូន</errorname> លេចឡើង?"

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:377
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you bind a mouse button to an external command as described in the <link "
"linkend=\"config\">Configuration</link> chapter, &ktimemon; does not check for "
"a valid command name. Instead a command shell is invoked to execute the "
"statement, so shell commands, environment variables and more can be used. To "
"allow some feedback to the user, &ktimemon; monitors the <systemitem>"
"stderr</systemitem> output of the command shell, and reports it in this message "
"box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: ktimemon.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While this scheme can be helpful in case a command is not found, it can be "
"quite annoying if the invoked command prints harmless diagnostic information on "
"<systemitem>stderr</systemitem>. A simple and elegant solution to this problem "
"is to add <userinput>2&gt;/dev/null</userinput> at the end of the command "
"specification. This redirects diagnostic messages to message nirvana, and stops "
"the message box popping up."
msgstr ""

